('qq-11-001','chapter_quiz','11','hair_care_services','What is the primary purpose of a shampoo service in Chapter 11?','To change the natural wave pattern before cutting','To cleanse the hair and scalp as part of service preparation','To replace the need for hair and scalp analysis','To prepare every client for a chemical service','b','Chapter 11 treats shampooing as cleansing the hair and scalp with a suitable product as part of safe service preparation.','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381',jsonb_build_object('repository_path','src/lib/chapter-11-premium-quiz.ts','repository_commit','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381','selection','po1c2_even_coverage','certification','current_premium_quiz'),'active'),
('qq-11-004','chapter_quiz','11','hair_care_services','Why is correct draping important during wet or chemical services?','It guarantees the service will take less time','It prevents the need for consultation','It allows stronger products to be used','It helps protect the client''s skin and clothing from liquids or chemicals','d','Chapter 11 identifies protection of the client''s skin and clothing as a central purpose of draping.','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381',jsonb_build_object('repository_path','src/lib/chapter-11-premium-quiz.ts','repository_commit','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381','selection','po1c2_even_coverage','certification','current_premium_quiz'),'active'),
('qq-11-006','chapter_quiz','11','hair_care_services','Which statement correctly describes the reclined shampoo method?','The client bends forward over the bowl','It is reserved only for clients with disabilities','It is the most common method and is used with a reclining or hydraulic chair','It is performed without a shampoo bowl','c','Chapter 11 identifies the reclined method as the most common shampoo method and associates it with a shampoo bowl and reclining or hydraulic chair.','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381',jsonb_build_object('repository_path','src/lib/chapter-11-premium-quiz.ts','repository_commit','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381','selection','po1c2_even_coverage','certification','current_premium_quiz'),'active'),
('qq-11-009','chapter_quiz','11','hair_care_services','What should happen before shampoo water is applied to the client?','The water should be made as hot as the barber can tolerate','The client should select the water temperature without testing','The water temperature should be tested for client comfort','The water should alternate between hot and cold','c','Chapter 11 specifically includes proper water-temperature testing in shampoo preparation.','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381',jsonb_build_object('repository_path','src/lib/chapter-11-premium-quiz.ts','repository_commit','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381','selection','po1c2_even_coverage','certification','current_premium_quiz'),'active'),
('qq-11-011','chapter_quiz','11','hair_care_services','What should occur before product selection and treatment setup?','Consultation and hair/scalp analysis','Scalp steam','Electric massage','Hair tonic application','a','Chapter 11 places consultation and hair/scalp analysis before product and treatment selection.','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381',jsonb_build_object('repository_path','src/lib/chapter-11-premium-quiz.ts','repository_commit','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381','selection','po1c2_even_coverage','certification','current_premium_quiz'),'active'),
('qq-11-014','chapter_quiz','11','hair_care_services','Which product match is supported for fine hair?','Heavy leave-in conditioner as the primary match','Only strong clarifying products','Volumizing shampoo, detangling conditioner, and protein treatments','No conditioner or treatment products','c','The Chapter 11 product table pairs fine hair with volumizing shampoo, detangling conditioner, and protein treatments.','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381',jsonb_build_object('repository_path','src/lib/chapter-11-premium-quiz.ts','repository_commit','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381','selection','po1c2_even_coverage','certification','current_premium_quiz'),'active'),
('qq-11-016','chapter_quiz','11','hair_care_services','Which product match is supported for coarse hair?','Volumizing shampoo only','Protein treatment only','Dry shampoo only','Moisturizing products and leave-in conditioners','d','The Chapter 11 product table pairs coarse hair with moisturizing products and leave-in conditioners.','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381',jsonb_build_object('repository_path','src/lib/chapter-11-premium-quiz.ts','repository_commit','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381','selection','po1c2_even_coverage','certification','current_premium_quiz'),'active'),
('qq-11-019','chapter_quiz','11','hair_care_services','Which description best matches a rotary scalp-massage movement?','Straight downward strokes with the palms','Rapid tapping with the fingertips','Hair pulling followed by release','Overlapping circular movement with thumbs or fingertips','d','The source describes rotary massage as overlapping circular movement performed with the thumbs or fingertips.','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381',jsonb_build_object('repository_path','src/lib/chapter-11-premium-quiz.ts','repository_commit','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381','selection','po1c2_even_coverage','certification','current_premium_quiz'),'active'),
('qq-11-022','chapter_quiz','11','hair_care_services','Where should Chapter 11 scalp-massage manipulations begin?','At the crown','Behind the ears','At the hairline','At the nape only','c','The source directs the barber to start at the hairline and use even, continuous, synchronized movement.','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381',jsonb_build_object('repository_path','src/lib/chapter-11-premium-quiz.ts','repository_commit','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381','selection','po1c2_even_coverage','certification','current_premium_quiz'),'active'),
('qq-11-024','chapter_quiz','11','hair_care_services','While massaging from behind the ears toward the crown, which movement choice matches the Chapter 11 table?','Back-and-forth only','Sliding only','Tapping followed by pulling','Rotary and sliding movements','d','The Chapter 11 massage table assigns rotary and sliding movements to the area behind the ears toward the crown.','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381',jsonb_build_object('repository_path','src/lib/chapter-11-premium-quiz.ts','repository_commit','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381','selection','po1c2_even_coverage','certification','current_premium_quiz'),'active'),
('qq-11-027','chapter_quiz','11','hair_care_services','Which condition does Chapter 11 associate with dry scalp?','Overactive sebaceous glands','Reduced activity of the oil glands','Excessive scalp steam','Frequent use of a hot towel','b','The Chapter 11 source summary associates dry scalp with inactivity or reduced activity of the oil glands.','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381',jsonb_build_object('repository_path','src/lib/chapter-11-premium-quiz.ts','repository_commit','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381','selection','po1c2_even_coverage','certification','current_premium_quiz'),'active'),
('qq-11-029','chapter_quiz','11','hair_care_services','Which organism does the Chapter 11 source summary associate with dandruff?','Malassezia','Staphylococcus','A parasitic mite','A bacterial condition unrelated to dandruff','a','The repository Chapter 11 source summary associates dandruff with Malassezia.','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381',jsonb_build_object('repository_path','src/lib/chapter-11-premium-quiz.ts','repository_commit','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381','selection','po1c2_even_coverage','certification','current_premium_quiz'),'active'),
('qq-11-032','chapter_quiz','11','hair_care_services','Which set consists entirely of services or equipment Chapter 11 includes in hair/scalp treatment?','Hair coloring, permanent waving, nail care, and shaving','Surgical removal, prescription medication, scalp injection, and massage','Haircutting, beard design, waxing, and chemical relaxing','Suitable shampooing, scalp steam, hand/electric massage, and source-listed light/current equipment','d','The source includes cleansing with suitable shampoo, scalp steam, hand or electrical massage, infrared/ultraviolet lamps or high-frequency current, and cosmetic antiseptics or ointments.','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381',jsonb_build_object('repository_path','src/lib/chapter-11-premium-quiz.ts','repository_commit','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381','selection','po1c2_even_coverage','certification','current_premium_quiz'),'active'),
('qq-11-035','chapter_quiz','11','hair_care_services','How should an electric massager be positioned before use?','In the palm with the fingers closed around it','On the back of the hand so the thumb and fingers remain free','At the wrist with the fingers immobilized','Against the scalp before the intensity is adjusted','b','The source directs the barber to adjust the electric massager on the back of the hand, leaving the thumb and fingers free.','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381',jsonb_build_object('repository_path','src/lib/chapter-11-premium-quiz.ts','repository_commit','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381','selection','po1c2_even_coverage','certification','current_premium_quiz'),'active'),
('qq-11-037','chapter_quiz','11','hair_care_services','Which sequence matches the Chapter 11 hair-tonic treatment?','Steam, shampoo, cut, massage, rinse','Massage, cut, tonic, rinse, steam','Apply tonic, massage, apply steam, massage again, comb into style','Shampoo, color, steam, condition, cut','c','The source sequence is tonic application, scalp massage, scalp steam, another massage by hand or vibrator, then combing into the desired style.','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381',jsonb_build_object('repository_path','src/lib/chapter-11-premium-quiz.ts','repository_commit','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381','selection','po1c2_even_coverage','certification','current_premium_quiz'),'active'),
('qq-11-040','chapter_quiz','11','hair_care_services','A scalp condition appears consistent with a staphylococcal infection. What is the Chapter 11 service decision?','Perform a short massage only','Apply cosmetic antiseptic and continue','Proceed if the client signs a waiver','Do not treat the disorder as a barber; refer the client to a physician','d','Staphylococcal scalp infections are specifically outside the barber''s treatment scope in Chapter 11.','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381',jsonb_build_object('repository_path','src/lib/chapter-11-premium-quiz.ts','repository_commit','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381','selection','po1c2_even_coverage','certification','current_premium_quiz'),'active'),
('qq-11-042','chapter_quiz','11','hair_care_services','A client asks the barber to medically treat a scalp disorder that Chapter 11 places outside barbering scope. What is the best response?','Treat it if the client has had it before','Decline the medical treatment and refer appropriately','Use an electric massager first to see whether it improves','Recommend a prescription-strength product','b','The barber should remain within cosmetic-service scope and refer conditions that require medical treatment.','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381',jsonb_build_object('repository_path','src/lib/chapter-11-premium-quiz.ts','repository_commit','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381','selection','po1c2_even_coverage','certification','current_premium_quiz'),'active'),
('qq-11-045','chapter_quiz','11','hair_care_services','Which product direction does Chapter 11 pair with wavy or curly hair?','Heavy oil only','Strong soap only','Light leave-in products and protein treatments','No conditioner or treatment','c','The Chapter 11 product table pairs wavy or curly hair with light leave-in products and protein treatments.','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381',jsonb_build_object('repository_path','src/lib/chapter-11-premium-quiz.ts','repository_commit','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381','selection','po1c2_even_coverage','certification','current_premium_quiz'),'active'),
('qq-11-047','chapter_quiz','11','hair_care_services','A client has coarse hair and asks which product direction fits the Chapter 11 table. Which answer is best?','Volumizing shampoo and no conditioner','Only pH-balanced products','Light leave-in products only','Moisturizing products and leave-in conditioners','d','Chapter 11 pairs coarse hair with moisturizing products and leave-in conditioners.','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381',jsonb_build_object('repository_path','src/lib/chapter-11-premium-quiz.ts','repository_commit','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381','selection','po1c2_even_coverage','certification','current_premium_quiz'),'active'),
('qq-11-050','chapter_quiz','11','hair_care_services','Which statement best describes the Chapter 11 professional boundary for scalp disorders?','Provide cosmetic maintenance within scope, but refer parasitic or staphylococcal disorders for medical care','Diagnose and treat any scalp disorder if the client agrees','Prescribe medication when cosmetic products do not work','Use massage to determine whether an infection is present','a','Chapter 11 permits cosmetic hair/scalp care within scope but specifically excludes treatment of parasitic and staphylococcal scalp disorders and directs referral to a physician.','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381',jsonb_build_object('repository_path','src/lib/chapter-11-premium-quiz.ts','repository_commit','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381','selection','po1c2_even_coverage','certification','current_premium_quiz'),'active'),
('qq-14-001','chapter_quiz','14','hair_care_services','What is the primary purpose of a client consultation before a haircut?','To determine the client''s desired look and assess hair and scalp conditions','To sell additional products and services','To determine how much to charge for the service','To check the client''s identification','a','The consultation determines the client''s desired look, assesses hair and scalp conditions, eliminates guesswork, and helps make informed professional judgments.','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381',jsonb_build_object('repository_path','src/lib/chapter-14-premium-quiz.ts','repository_commit','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381','selection','po1c2_even_coverage','certification','current_premium_quiz'),'active'),
('qq-14-004','chapter_quiz','14','hair_care_services','What does a client typically mean when they ask for ''just a trim''?','They want a completely different style','They want the cheapest service available','They want only the bangs cut','They want to retain length, not remove significant hair','d','"Just a trim" usually means the client wants to retain length. It may mean an outline cleanup, a taper trim, or simply less hair removed — always clarify exact expectations.','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381',jsonb_build_object('repository_path','src/lib/chapter-14-premium-quiz.ts','repository_commit','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381','selection','po1c2_even_coverage','certification','current_premium_quiz'),'active'),
('qq-14-008','chapter_quiz','14','hair_care_services','A client with a round face wants a haircut that creates a more balanced appearance. What design goal should guide the barber?','Add width to the sides','Emphasize fullness','Keep hair very short all over','Create the illusion of length and slimming','d','For a round face, the goal is to create the illusion of length and slimming. Add height on top, use off-center parts, and avoid very short hair that emphasizes fullness.','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381',jsonb_build_object('repository_path','src/lib/chapter-14-premium-quiz.ts','repository_commit','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381','selection','po1c2_even_coverage','certification','current_premium_quiz'),'active'),
('qq-14-011','chapter_quiz','14','hair_care_services','What is the three-zone method for facial shape analysis?','Left side, center, right side','Top, middle, bottom of the head','Forehead to eyebrows, eyebrows to nose, nose to chin','Eyes, nose, mouth','c','The three-zone method divides the face into three horizontal zones: forehead to eyebrows, eyebrows to end of nose, and end of nose to chin. This helps determine facial structure and guide style selection.','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381',jsonb_build_object('repository_path','src/lib/chapter-14-premium-quiz.ts','repository_commit','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381','selection','po1c2_even_coverage','certification','current_premium_quiz'),'active'),
('qq-14-014','chapter_quiz','14','hair_care_services','What is the design strategy for a concave profile?','Keep hair close at the forehead','Add volume over the forehead and suggest a beard','Use short hair all over','Avoid facial hair','b','For a concave profile, add volume over the forehead and suggest a beard or goatee to add bulk and balance the lower face.','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381',jsonb_build_object('repository_path','src/lib/chapter-14-premium-quiz.ts','repository_commit','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381','selection','po1c2_even_coverage','certification','current_premium_quiz'),'active'),
('qq-14-017','chapter_quiz','14','hair_care_services','A client has protruding ears and wants a haircut that makes them less noticeable. Which design approach is most appropriate?','Leave hair fuller on the sides or cover the top of the ears','Cut hair very short around the ears','Shave the sides completely','Use a high fade to expose the ears','a','For protruding ears, minimize attention by leaving hair fuller on the sides or choosing styles that cover the top of the ears. This reduces the visible distance between the ear and the head.','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381',jsonb_build_object('repository_path','src/lib/chapter-14-premium-quiz.ts','repository_commit','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381','selection','po1c2_even_coverage','certification','current_premium_quiz'),'active'),
('qq-14-021','chapter_quiz','14','hair_care_services','What is tapering?','The gradual increase of hair length without visible lines of demarcation','Cutting all hair to the same length','Removing bulk from the interior of the haircut','Creating sharp, defined lines in the haircut','a','Tapering is the gradual increase of hair length from one point to another without visible lines of demarcation (gaps or steps).','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381',jsonb_build_object('repository_path','src/lib/chapter-14-premium-quiz.ts','repository_commit','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381','selection','po1c2_even_coverage','certification','current_premium_quiz'),'active'),
('qq-14-024','chapter_quiz','14','hair_care_services','What effect do horizontal lines create in a haircut?','Remove weight and create layers','Create sloped lines within the design','Soften the overall appearance','Build weight and create one-length looks','d','Horizontal lines build weight and are used to create one-length looks and low-elevation or blunt designs. Weight lines are usually created at the perimeter or occipital area.','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381',jsonb_build_object('repository_path','src/lib/chapter-14-premium-quiz.ts','repository_commit','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381','selection','po1c2_even_coverage','certification','current_premium_quiz'),'active'),
('qq-14-027','chapter_quiz','14','hair_care_services','How does color create illusions in haircut design?','Dark colors add volume; light colors reduce volume','Color has no effect on perceived depth','Dark colors recede; lighter colors appear to come forward','Only bright colors create illusions','c','Dark colors appear to recede in a design, while lighter colors appear to come forward. This creates illusions of depth and volume.','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381',jsonb_build_object('repository_path','src/lib/chapter-14-premium-quiz.ts','repository_commit','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381','selection','po1c2_even_coverage','certification','current_premium_quiz'),'active'),
('qq-14-031','chapter_quiz','14','hair_care_services','When is 180-degree elevation used?','For very short buzz cuts','For outlining the perimeter','For long hair where a 90-degree guide is insufficient','For texturizing the ends','c','180-degree elevation is used for long hair where a 90-degree guide is insufficient. The hair being cut is at 180 degrees, not the stationary guide itself.','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381',jsonb_build_object('repository_path','src/lib/chapter-14-premium-quiz.ts','repository_commit','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381','selection','po1c2_even_coverage','certification','current_premium_quiz'),'active'),
('qq-14-034','chapter_quiz','14','hair_care_services','What is cross-checking?','Checking the client''s ID before service','Verifying accuracy by parting subsections opposite from the original cutting direction','Using two mirrors to see the back of the head','Asking the client to approve the haircut','b','Cross-checking is the process of verifying accuracy by parting off subsections opposite from the original elevation or cutting direction. For example, a vertical subsection cut at 90 degrees can be verified by parting horizontally at 90 degrees.','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381',jsonb_build_object('repository_path','src/lib/chapter-14-premium-quiz.ts','repository_commit','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381','selection','po1c2_even_coverage','certification','current_premium_quiz'),'active'),
('qq-14-037','chapter_quiz','14','hair_care_services','What is texturizing?','A technique performed after the main cut to create special effects','The process of washing the hair before cutting','A method of outlining the perimeter','A type of clipper blade','a','Texturizing is a technique performed after the main cut to create special effects such as wispy or spiky strands. It can be performed within the interior or along the perimeter.','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381',jsonb_build_object('repository_path','src/lib/chapter-14-premium-quiz.ts','repository_commit','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381','selection','po1c2_even_coverage','certification','current_premium_quiz'),'active'),
('qq-14-040','chapter_quiz','14','hair_care_services','What is the difference between a cutting line and a design line?','They are the same thing','A cutting line is for shears; a design line is for clippers','A cutting line is temporary; a design line is permanent','A cutting line is the angle of fingers or comb; a design line is the outer perimeter of the finished haircut','d','A cutting line is the angle established by fingers or comb when securing a section. A design line is the outer perimeter of the finished haircut.','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381',jsonb_build_object('repository_path','src/lib/chapter-14-premium-quiz.ts','repository_commit','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381','selection','po1c2_even_coverage','certification','current_premium_quiz'),'active'),
('qq-14-044','chapter_quiz','14','hair_care_services','Where is the shear-over-comb technique primarily used?','Only on the top of the head','Only for creating fades','Only for texturizing','The nape, behind ears, around ears, and sideburns','d','The shear-over-comb technique is primarily used for cutting hair ends and executing tapers in the nape, behind the ears, around the ears, and in the sideburn areas.','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381',jsonb_build_object('repository_path','src/lib/chapter-14-premium-quiz.ts','repository_commit','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381','selection','po1c2_even_coverage','certification','current_premium_quiz'),'active'),
('qq-14-047','chapter_quiz','14','hair_care_services','What is arching with a clipper or trimmer?','Creating a curved part in the hair','Removing bulk from the crown','Outlining sideburns and neck with a fine cutting edge for precision','Blending the fade transition','c','Arching is a method to clean up and outline sideburns and the neck outline using the fine cutting edge of a smaller cutting head. It is efficient, precise, and ideal for detailed work around ears and neck sides.','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381',jsonb_build_object('repository_path','src/lib/chapter-14-premium-quiz.ts','repository_commit','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381','selection','po1c2_even_coverage','certification','current_premium_quiz'),'active'),
('qq-14-050','chapter_quiz','14','hair_care_services','When using a wet-razor haircutting procedure, why is even moisture important?','It guarantees the haircut will dry to the exact same length','It supports smoother, controlled cutting and client comfort','It eliminates the need for sectioning','It is a universal licensing requirement','b','Consistent moisture can support smoother, controlled cutting and client comfort. Follow the procedure, manufacturer guidance, and instructor direction for the razor technique being used.','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381',jsonb_build_object('repository_path','src/lib/chapter-14-premium-quiz.ts','repository_commit','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381','selection','po1c2_even_coverage','certification','current_premium_quiz'),'active'),
('qq-14-054','chapter_quiz','14','hair_care_services','What is carving in haircutting?','Cutting hair with a razor in a curved line','Elevating hair at 45–90 degrees and gliding open shears with a curving motion','Creating a design in the hair with clippers','Removing bulk from the top surface','b','Carving is elevating hair at 45–90 degrees and gliding open shears with a curving motion to remove bulk from the under-portion of the parting, continuing the motion to the hair ends.','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381',jsonb_build_object('repository_path','src/lib/chapter-14-premium-quiz.ts','repository_commit','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381','selection','po1c2_even_coverage','certification','current_premium_quiz'),'active'),
('qq-14-057','chapter_quiz','14','hair_care_services','What are the characteristics of a flat top haircut?','Very short sides with a flat, squared-off top section','Long hair on top with tapered sides','Even length all over the head','Curved top with short sides','a','A flat top has very short sides and back with slightly longer hair at the upper parietal and front sections. The top section is flat and squared-off when viewed from the front.','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381',jsonb_build_object('repository_path','src/lib/chapter-14-premium-quiz.ts','repository_commit','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381','selection','po1c2_even_coverage','certification','current_premium_quiz'),'active'),
('qq-14-060','chapter_quiz','14','hair_care_services','What is a pomp fade?','A fade with a hard part','A taper with a curved top','A crew cut with a fade','A combination of very short fade sides with an extra long top','d','A pomp fade is a modern variation that combines very short nape, back, and side sections of a fade with the extra long top section of a classic pompadour.','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381',jsonb_build_object('repository_path','src/lib/chapter-14-premium-quiz.ts','repository_commit','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381','selection','po1c2_even_coverage','certification','current_premium_quiz'),'active'),
('qq-14-063','chapter_quiz','14','hair_care_services','Which activity is an example of optional finish work after a haircut?','Skipping the final visual check','Changing the haircut without client agreement','Outlining or neck cleanup based on the service plan and client preference','Using the same finishing step for every client regardless of the service','c','Finish work depends on the service plan, client preference, scope, and local practice. It may include outlining, neck cleanup, eyebrow grooming, or removal of stray hairs as appropriate.','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381',jsonb_build_object('repository_path','src/lib/chapter-14-premium-quiz.ts','repository_commit','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381','selection','po1c2_even_coverage','certification','current_premium_quiz'),'active'),
('qq-14-067','chapter_quiz','14','hair_care_services','What is the most accurate statement about how long lock development takes?','It always finishes in exactly 6 to 12 months','It always finishes within two weeks','It varies with hair characteristics, method, maintenance, and time','It follows one fixed timeline for every client','c','Lock development varies by hair characteristics, technique, maintenance, and time, so a universal completion timeline should not be promised.','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381',jsonb_build_object('repository_path','src/lib/chapter-14-premium-quiz.ts','repository_commit','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381','selection','po1c2_even_coverage','certification','current_premium_quiz'),'active'),
('qq-14-070','chapter_quiz','14','hair_care_services','What is the critical blowdrying safety rule?','Hold the dryer as close to the scalp as possible','Continuously move both the dryer and the hair to prevent scalp burns','Use the highest heat setting for fastest results','Focus heat on one section until completely dry','b','The critical blowdrying safety rule is to continuously move both the blowdryer air stream and the hair being dried. Never hold the dryer stationary on one spot to avoid burning the client''s scalp.','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381',jsonb_build_object('repository_path','src/lib/chapter-14-premium-quiz.ts','repository_commit','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381','selection','po1c2_even_coverage','certification','current_premium_quiz'),'active'),
('qq-18-01','chapter_quiz','18','hair_care_services','Which group of observations gives the strongest foundation for planning a haircolor or lightening service?','Length, haircut shape, styling preference, and product fragrance','Hair integrity/elasticity, texture, density, porosity, natural level/tone, and contributing pigment','Only the client’s desired shade and the formula used at the last visit','Only scalp oiliness and the amount of gray hair','b','Haircolor planning should start with a broad hair and scalp analysis. Integrity/elasticity, texture, density, porosity, natural level/tone, and contributing pigment all influence service planning. No single trait should automatically determine developer strength or processing time; the product system and hair condition still control those choices.','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381',jsonb_build_object('repository_path','src/lib/chapter-18-premium-quiz.ts','repository_commit','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381','selection','po1c2_even_coverage','certification','current_premium_quiz'),'active'),
('qq-18-03','chapter_quiz','18','hair_care_services','Which statement about professional haircolor level systems is most accurate?','Every manufacturer must use exactly 1 for black and 10 for the lightest blond','Level describes how light or dark a color is, but exact numbering and shade names can vary by manufacturer','Level describes only whether a tone is warm or cool','Level numbers are interchangeable with developer volumes','b','Level describes relative lightness or darkness. Many professional lines use numbered scales, but the exact numbering, endpoints, and shade names can vary. Use the specific manufacturer’s swatch book or technical chart rather than treating one numbering system as universal.','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381',jsonb_build_object('repository_path','src/lib/chapter-18-premium-quiz.ts','repository_commit','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381','selection','po1c2_even_coverage','certification','current_premium_quiz'),'active'),
('qq-18-04','chapter_quiz','18','hair_care_services','Which description best fits temporary haircolor as a product category?','A short-duration color effect that primarily deposits color near the hair surface, with longevity that varies by formula and hair condition','A permanent oxidative system that always lifts natural pigment','A lightener that removes natural melanin before a toner is applied','A demipermanent system that must always be mixed with 20-volume developer','a','Temporary haircolor is intended for short-duration color effects and generally deposits color near the hair surface. How quickly it shampoos out depends on the specific product, hair condition, and use, so a universal one-shampoo rule should not be promised.','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381',jsonb_build_object('repository_path','src/lib/chapter-18-premium-quiz.ts','repository_commit','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381','selection','po1c2_even_coverage','certification','current_premium_quiz'),'active'),
('qq-18-06','chapter_quiz','18','hair_care_services','A client has unwanted orange warmth at a level where blue is the appropriate complementary relationship. Which tonal direction is used to reduce the orange?','Gold','Red-orange','Blue','Yellow','c','Complementary color relationships are used to reduce unwanted tonal influence. Blue is complementary to orange in traditional haircolor theory. The final formula still has to match the client’s level, underlying pigment, target tone, and the professional color system being used.','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381',jsonb_build_object('repository_path','src/lib/chapter-18-premium-quiz.ts','repository_commit','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381','selection','po1c2_even_coverage','certification','current_premium_quiz'),'active'),
('qq-18-07','chapter_quiz','18','hair_care_services','Very porous lengths are expected to take color differently from the less-porous regrowth. What is the most appropriate planning step before choosing a darker formula?','Automatically choose a formula one to two levels lighter for every porous client','Use a stronger developer so all areas absorb color equally','Assess the porosity difference, use a strand test when appropriate, and follow the color system’s porosity/equalization guidance','Ignore porosity because it does not affect color uptake','c','Porous hair can take up color unevenly, but there is no universal rule to compensate by automatically choosing a fixed number of levels lighter or by increasing developer strength. Analyze the hair, use a strand test when appropriate, and use the manufacturer-supported porosity or equalization strategy.','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381',jsonb_build_object('repository_path','src/lib/chapter-18-premium-quiz.ts','repository_commit','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381','selection','po1c2_even_coverage','certification','current_premium_quiz'),'active'),
('qq-18-09','chapter_quiz','18','hair_care_services','During a lightener retouch, what is the safest general placement principle?','Apply lightener from scalp to ends on every retouch','Target the new growth and avoid unapproved overlap onto previously lightened or sensitized hair','Pull lightener through all previously lightened lengths during the final minutes','Apply only to the ends because regrowth lifts on its own','b','Previously lightened hair can be more vulnerable to damage. A retouch generally targets new growth while avoiding unapproved overlap onto previously lightened or sensitized hair. The specific product’s overlap, scalp, developer, and timing directions remain controlling.','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381',jsonb_build_object('repository_path','src/lib/chapter-18-premium-quiz.ts','repository_commit','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381','selection','po1c2_even_coverage','certification','current_premium_quiz'),'active'),
('qq-18-10','chapter_quiz','18','hair_care_services','A service plan intentionally lightens the hair first and then applies a separate toner or color to refine the final tone. What is this two-step structure called?','Single-process haircoloring','Double-process haircoloring','Temporary color application','Retouch-only color','b','Double-process haircoloring uses a separate lightening step followed by a separate toning or color step. Whether that approach is suitable for a particular client depends on the target result, starting level, hair integrity, and the product systems being used.','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381',jsonb_build_object('repository_path','src/lib/chapter-18-premium-quiz.ts','repository_commit','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381','selection','po1c2_even_coverage','certification','current_premium_quiz'),'active'),
('qq-18-12','chapter_quiz','18','hair_care_services','Which statement best reflects current FDA guidance and federal hair-dye requirements about allergy/skin testing?','Federal law creates one universal 24–48-hour timing rule for every haircolor product','A skin test is unnecessary if the client has used the same color before','Follow the product’s exact allergy-alert or skin-test directions; FDA advises a skin test before each hair-dye use, while qualifying coal-tar hair dyes have specific caution-label and preliminary-test requirements','Only permanent color products can cause allergic reactions','c','FDA advises users and salons to perform a skin test before each hair-dye use and to follow package directions. Federal law separately gives qualifying coal-tar hair dyes special treatment when required caution labeling and adequate preliminary-test directions are provided. Do not replace those product-specific directions with one invented universal timing rule.','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381',jsonb_build_object('repository_path','src/lib/chapter-18-premium-quiz.ts','repository_commit','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381','selection','po1c2_even_coverage','certification','current_premium_quiz'),'active'),
('qq-18-13','chapter_quiz','18','hair_care_services','Which rule should govern coloring a client’s beard or mustache?','Any scalp haircolor is acceptable if petroleum jelly is applied first','Any off-scalp powder lightener is acceptable on facial hair','Use only a product whose manufacturer expressly permits the intended beard or mustache application, and follow its allergy-alert, skin, timing, rinsing, and eye-area precautions','Metallic or progressive dyes are always the safest facial-hair option','c','Do not transfer scalp-hair directions to facial hair by assumption. A beard or mustache color service should use a product expressly permitted for that intended facial-hair application and should follow that product’s warnings and application procedure exactly.','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381',jsonb_build_object('repository_path','src/lib/chapter-18-premium-quiz.ts','repository_commit','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381','selection','po1c2_even_coverage','certification','current_premium_quiz'),'active'),
('qq-18-15','chapter_quiz','18','hair_care_services','Previously lightened, highly porous lengths are being tinted back darker and are likely to take color differently from the regrowth. What is the best first planning step?','Automatically apply 40-volume developer to the porous lengths','Ignore the porosity difference and apply one formula everywhere','Assess the hair, use a strand test when appropriate, and choose a manufacturer-supported tint-back, filler, or equalization strategy for the target result','Skip allergy-alert testing because the hair has already been chemically processed','c','Tint-back work on porous hair may require replacement of missing underlying tone, a filler, or another equalization strategy, but there is no single universal formula. Analyze the hair, consider a strand test, and use the product system’s supported tint-back or filler guidance.','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381',jsonb_build_object('repository_path','src/lib/chapter-18-premium-quiz.ts','repository_commit','15dc88e5561d05004a066d22a9c7c1e1e095d381','selection','po1c2_even_coverage','certification','current_premium_quiz'),'active')
